  "description": "GETRII crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H168 Ce6 Fe4 N4 O44,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Ce1 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.192-3.923 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.09-129.12°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Fe4Ce6O8(hmpip)4((CH3)3CCO2)12(CH3CO2)4]·CH3CN.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
